@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option desk - Licensing (PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0, one licence over the whole repository)

component "Noncommercial use\npersonal study, research, hobby,\ncharities, schools, public research,\nhealth, environment, government,\nwhatever their funding" as free #C6E9C6
component "Option desk\nengine, shell, agent, skills,\ncommands, dashboard" as work
component "Commercial use\nfunds and trading businesses,\nselling it or access to it, paid\nconsulting or signals, courses,\nfundraising on the back of it" as paid

free --> work : no permission needed
paid ..> work : written agreement first

note bottom of free
Modify it, build on it, pass it on,
as long as these terms travel with it.
end note

note bottom of paid
Ask: terms are negotiable and
a share is one of the shapes
they take.
end note

note right of work
Deliberately not OSI open source,
and the trade is named: fewer users,
fewer contributors, some directories
treat noncommercial as unfree.
The previous MIT + AGPL pair allowed
the exact thing it was meant to stop.
Copies taken before 2026-08-31 keep
the terms they were given.
end note

caption Full detail in LICENSES.md; provenance of every borrowed line in THIRD-PARTY.md; contribution terms in CLA.md.
@enduml
